# Git agent gates

Canonical detail: [docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md](docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md).

## Commit timing on spec branches (`T-XX-YY-ZZ`)

- **Do not** run `git commit` (or amend) on a spec branch until **`openspec archive`** has completed for that change.
- TDD work stays **uncommitted** until then; staging for review is OK.
- If the user asks to commit before archive, **refuse**, cite [docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md](docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md) (regla de commit), and offer archive first (tests green + user OK for archive).

## Forbidden without explicit user authorization

- `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or any commit that stages and commits in one flow (on spec branches: only **after** archive, per above)
- Creating or merging Pull Requests (`gh pr create`, etc.)
- Pushing a branch **for the purpose of opening a PR** the user did not request

Staging files for the user's review is allowed unless the user forbids it.

## Proactive proposals (required)

When gates are met, **always propose** the next Git action; do **not** wait for the user to ask.

**Commit proposal** (include in the message):

- List of paths to stage (or confirm `git status` summary).
- Full suggested message ([Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/), see doc § 7).
- One-line rationale.
- Explicit question: e.g. *¿Autorizás que ejecute este commit?*

**When to propose a commit**

- Spec branch `T-XX-YY-ZZ`: only **after** `openspec archive` (see commit timing above).
- Legacy / entrega branches (e.g. `feature/entrega-1-DPM`): when a coherent slice of work is done and the tree has changes worth versioning.
- Never propose a commit that violates post-archive rules on spec branches.

**PR proposal** (after the branch has the commit(s) to integrate, or will after the proposed commit):

- **Base:** `develop` (unless the user specifies otherwise).
- **Head:** current branch name.
- Suggested **title** (Conventional Commits, aligned with main commit).
- Short **body** (ticket/spec, archive status, tests run) per doc § 9.
- Note if **`git push -u origin HEAD`** is needed first; propose push only with separate authorization unless the user bundles it with PR approval.
- Explicit question: e.g. *¿Autorizás que cree el PR (y push si hace falta)?*

Do **not** run `git commit`, `git push`, or `gh pr create` until the user answers yes to that proposal.

## Authorization

- Treat authorization as **explicit in the current conversation** (e.g. "sí, hacé el commit", "abrí el PR").
- A prior "yes" does not authorize a **different** commit message or PR than the one proposed.
- When in doubt, ask; do not assume prior messages authorize a new commit or PR.

## After authorization

- Proposed and actual commit messages MUST follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) per [docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md](docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md) § 7.
- Use scope `(T-XX-YY-ZZ)` matching the branch; footer `Refs: T-XX-YY` for the parent ticket when helpful.
- PR titles should use the same convention as the primary commit subject.
- Never force-push to `main` unless the user explicitly requests it.
